f 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c9cd435-4b0a-516c-bede-18c713c259dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343389" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-5{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-3,3).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $6$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}∼-15+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{180(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3}∼-15x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}\\right).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-15+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{180(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-3,3).$ \nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-5{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-15+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{180(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi t}{3}\\right))\\text{d}t \\\\ {[-\\frac{5}{3}{t}^{3}]}_{0}^{x} & ∼[-15t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{180(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{3}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi t}{3}\\right)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{3} & ∼-15x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{540(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}{\\pi }^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425679 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37c65c3f-51c2-5a52-94fb-939ac7507bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425576} {:answer/id #uuid "4c976545-3bb9-5b3a-96f5-f4efde761a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425585} {:answer/id #uuid "a10e5066-a255-5a58-8bdc-c8135fc299f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425610} {:answer/id #uuid "df8883ad-be27-5c96-80f9-a6c82c5de1fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df8883ad-be27-5c96-80f9-a6c82c5de1fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425627} :answer-field/id #uuid "04ad8b60-8a46-572e-9c0d-e6fe2e8f69a7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097c8db1-3ed4-5c62-8384-75b3665d2464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425549} {:answer/id #uuid "31e037d0-6ce2-5da7-a3c6-2e20090807e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425